# # /docs/
#
# The w3id.org documentation site.
#
# https://w3id.org/docs/ redirects to https://docs.w3id.org/
# https://w3id.org/docs/guides/create-an-id redirects to
# https://docs.w3id.org/guides/create-an-id
#
# The site is built from the `docs/` directory of this repository and published
# to GitHub Pages. A 302 is used rather than a 301 because the layout of the
# documentation site is expected to change over time, and a cached permanent
# redirect cannot be taken back.
#
# NOTE: do not add `DirectorySlash Off` or `Options -Indexes` to this file.
# This is a real directory, so Apache first redirects /docs to /docs/ and the
# rule below then handles the request. Turning DirectorySlash off would stop
# the rule from running for the bare /docs URL and would produce a 403 instead.
# See https://w3id.org/docs/rules/htaccess/no-options-directive
#
# ## Contact
# This space is administered by:
#
# W3C Permanent Identifier Community Group
# public-perma-id@w3.org
# https://www.w3.org/community/perma-id/
# GitHub organization: perma-id

RewriteEngine on

# Pass the whole path through, so that https://w3id.org/docs/llms.txt and
# https://w3id.org/docs/rules/htaccess/https-target resolve too.
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://docs.w3id.org/$1 [R=302,L]
